{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "CHO fed-batch media supplement screening",
  "notes": "Screening of ten supplements added to a chemically defined basal medium for a CHO-K1 cell line producing an IgG1 antibody. Each run is a 125 mL shake flask (30 mL working volume, 14-day fed batch, 36.5 °C set point, 5 % CO2, 125 rpm). Flasks were run in three incubators over two weeks; the mean deviation of the logged flask-zone temperature from the set point is recorded for each flask. Titre is the day-14 Protein A HPLC result and peak viable cell density the highest daily count (trypan blue, automated counter). The goal is to find the few supplements worth carrying into a response-surface study.",
  "factors": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "symbol": "A",
      "name": "Glucose",
      "units": "g/L",
      "kind": {
        "type": "continuous",
        "low": 4.0,
        "high": 8.0
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
